<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Ukrainian People's Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1917 CE – 1921 CE · capital Kyiv</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Ukrainian national republic born in the Russian Revolution, which declared independence in 1918 and fought for its survival until 1921.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In March 1917 Ukrainian parties formed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-rada">Central Rada</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a>, chaired by the historian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mykhailo-hrushevsky">Mykhailo Hrushevsky</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/october-revolution">October Revolution</a> its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-universal">Third Universal</a> of November 1917 proclaimed the Ukrainian People's Republic, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-universal">Fourth Universal</a> of January 1918 declared full independence.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-rada">Rada</a> passed land reform and made a separate peace with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-powers">Central Powers</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-brest-litovsk">Brest-Litovsk</a> in February 1918, relying on German troops against the Bolsheviks. In April 1918 the Germans replaced it with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ukrainian-state">Ukrainian State</a>, but in December a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/directorate-of-ukraine">Directorate</a> led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volodymyr-vynnychenko">Volodymyr Vynnychenko</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/symon-petliura">Symon Petliura</a> restored the republic. In January 1919 it proclaimed union with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/west-ukrainian-peoples-republic">West Ukrainian People's Republic</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Attacked by Bolsheviks, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-movement">Whites</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poles">Poles</a>, the republic lost most of its territory in 1919. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/symon-petliura">Petliura</a> allied with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/second-polish-republic">Second Polish Republic</a> in 1920, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-riga">Peace of Riga</a> in 1921 divided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ukrainian-ssr">Ukrainian SSR</a>. The government continued in exile until 1992.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ukrainian-peoples-republic.jpg" alt="Ukrainian People's Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Original: Unknown author Vector: Ιγκόρ · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Ukraine_(1917%E2%80%931921).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1917 CE – 1921 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kyiv</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mykhailo Hrushevsky, Volodymyr Vynnychenko, Symon Petliura</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ukrainian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ukraine">Ukraine</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>UNR, Ukrainian National Republic</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1919&amp;focus=ukrainian-peoples-republic" aria-label="Ukrainian People's Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5377 425 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ukrainian People's Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5697 681L5635 424M5697 681L5697 681M5697 681L5697 681M5697 681L5551 699M5697 681L5745 719"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5635 424h0M5697 681h0M5697 681h0M5551 699h0M5745 719h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5697 681h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5697 681h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kyiv. <a href="/atlas?year=1919&amp;focus=ukrainian-peoples-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
